render/allocator: add allocator_autocreate_with_drm_fd()

wlr_allocator_autocreate() picks an allocator from a backend's buffer
capabilities and DRM FD. Split out the part that takes the capabilities and
the FD themselves, so that the DRM backend can create an allocator for the
buffers one GPU scans out, whatever else the backend accepts.

No functional change.

diff --git a/include/render/allocator/allocator.h b/include/render/allocator/allocator.h
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..cf846bb1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/render/allocator/allocator.h
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+#ifndef RENDER_ALLOCATOR_ALLOCATOR_H
+#define RENDER_ALLOCATOR_ALLOCATOR_H
+
+#include <stdint.h>
+#include <wlr/render/allocator.h>
+
+/**
+ * Creates an allocator for buffers that a backend with the given buffer
+ * capabilities can present, from the DRM device drm_fd refers to if it needs
+ * one (drm_fd may be negative if there is none).
+ */
+struct wlr_allocator *allocator_autocreate_with_drm_fd(uint32_t backend_caps,
+	struct wlr_renderer *renderer, int drm_fd);
+
+#endif
